### 4.2 Module Descriptions

**4.2.1 Physical World.** A multi-channel robotic liquid handler equipped with: 8 independent pipetting channels with z-axis control, tip ejectors, and wash stations; meniscus cameras (1280×960 px, 60 fps); weigh cells (0.1 mg resolution); pressure transducers (0.1 mbar resolution); conductivity probes; temperature sensors; and safety hardware including collision detection and emergency stop relays. All sensor data is transmitted over a deterministic EtherCAT bus with guaranteed latency < 1 ms.

**4.2.2 Edge Gateway Modules.** The Particle Filter (Manifold-Adaptive) maintains N = 10,000 particles with local PCA projection onto the estimated intrinsic manifold, outputting belief states at 100 Hz. The Calibrated Detector (GEMS-DFA) implements the discounted Dirichlet predictor and compiles it into a DFA with ε_DFA = 10⁻⁴, having approximately 10⁶ states and running in O(1) time per observation. The HITree Engine executes 47 verified correction protocols; each HITree node executes only if its KeYmaera X-verified dL guard is satisfied, on a real-time OS with a 10 ms control cycle. The Safe RL Policy uses DDPG augmented with the symbolically regressed Lyapunov shield; actions violating the shield are projected onto the safe set via quadratic programming. The Active Inference Module runs natural gradient descent at 10 Hz, providing pre-emptive maintenance recommendations. The LLM Agent is invoked only when DFA confidence is below threshold; its outputs are bounded by the verified fallback HITree.

**4.2.3 Cloud Modules.** The Federated Aggregator implements coordinate-wise median aggregation with Lyapunov witness verification, running daily with DP parameters (ε_DP = 1, δ_DP = 10⁻⁵). The Verified Recipe Book is a version-controlled repository of all 47 HITree correction protocols, each with an associated Isabelle/HOL proof. The Digital Twin is a dL-verified hybrid automaton run at 10× real-time for training data generation, with domain randomisation over 12 physical parameters.

### 4.3 Data Flow

1. Raw sensor data flows from the Physical World to the Particle Filter at 100 Hz.
2. The Particle Filter emits belief states to the Calibrated Detector, Safe RL Policy, and Active Inference module.
3. The Calibrated Detector converts belief states and observation history into a DFA state determining the error class.
4. The error class selects the appropriate HITree from the Verified Recipe Book.
5. The HITree Engine executes the HITree, invoking Safe RL actions (shielded) or Active Inference pre-emptive maintenance as needed.
6. Commands are sent to the liquid handler actuators.
7. Logs are transmitted to the Cloud for federated aggregation and recipe book expansion.

